# Input hotkeys — Ctrl / Numpad architecture

## Failure mode (2026-08-25)

Calling Rewired / `InputManager` (`NewPlayer`, `GetButton*`, Incremental action IDs) from YMS before the world is ready can corrupt `ControlBindings.json` (dead mouse). Stay on Unity `KeyCode` only. Do **not** write or clear DV binds from the mod. Do **not** make players rebind around us.

## Architecture (zero collision by design)

| Class | Keys | Modifier |
|-------|------|----------|
| **Gameplay** | Numpad `+` or Enter (reverser), Numpad `.` (TM fuse) | **None** — vanilla DV leaves the numpad unmapped |
| **UI / tools** | Home, End, F8 | **Ctrl** (Left **or** Right) held; Shift still means clear for Home/End |

Use the same inclusive Control check as Shift already does:

`Input.GetKey(KeyCode.LeftControl) || Input.GetKey(KeyCode.RightControl)`  
→ Core: `YmsHotkeyPolicy.ControlHeld` / `ShouldAcceptToolChord`.

## Current ship keys

| Chord / key | Feature |
|-------------|---------|
| **Numpad `+`** (Enter still works) | Cycle reverser N→R→F (wagon write) |
| **Numpad .** | TM fuse ON (numpad only — not main `.`) |
| **Ctrl+Home** / **Ctrl+Shift+Home** | Park mark set / clear |
| **Ctrl+End** / **Ctrl+Shift+End** | Path dest set / clear |
| **Ctrl+F8** | License debug grant/restore |
| **Ctrl+Insert** | Maps desk (city / track / Set dest) |

## Hard rules

1. Unity `GetKey*` only — never `InputManager` / Rewired action IDs for mod hotkeys.
2. Gate gameplay/tool polls until `HudWorldSession` + `ScreenOverlayGate.WorldReady()`.
3. New **tool** hotkeys → Ctrl chord via `YmsHotkeyPolicy`. New **gameplay** hotkeys → prefer unused **Numpad** keys.
4. Do not add main-keyboard Period/Home/End/F8 without Ctrl (regression).
5. Do not “unbind DV maps” from code to free a key.
